## Findings — neither blocking

- **F1 (C2) — SHOULD-FIX, commit-hygiene only.** C2's message lists `ResultIsInformative` as a
  new/exported helper; it **pre-exists at base** (`analyzer_helpers.go:53`, already exported, already
  called at `engine_v2.go:215`). `bindingAnchor` merely reuses it. Coder rewords before push; **no
  code change**. Violates the CONVENTIONS "commit message reflects the diff" rule (prose-only, minor).
- **F2 (C3) — NTH, test-coverage.** Plan Test 4's *"assert replicas unchanged + metric emitted"*
  clause is asserted by neither Test 4B (no-decision+no-panic) nor Test 5 (logged-refusal + empty
  QueryCallCounts). The cheap `NumReplicas`-unchanged half is directly addressable in Test 5; the
  metric half was flagged fragile by the coder (package-private gauge). Weigh at push-ready.

